# Lowmouth Bayou: a serpentine through the delta, folding back on itself
# the way the old channel does. Units in metres: x east, z south.
#
# North up the parish street by St. Anne's; east along the top of the
# levee with the river below; across the breach, where the Marrow broke
# through, on a pad and a lip, or into the deep water; south into the cane,
# every corner blind; west through the back swamp on cypress boardwalks with
# no rails over shallow water (a kart that falls in drives out up a log);
# through the hull of the Belle Marrow where she lies on the old channel;
# a mud stretch; and back through the tombs to the line.
track lowmouth_bayou size 768 style bayou
title LOWMOUTH BAYOU
blurb A humid summer morning in the delta, fog on the water: the levee top with the river below, a jump across the breach, blind bends through the cane, railless boardwalks over the cypress swamp and a run through a wrecked steamboat's hull.
race laps 3 rivals 5 vehicle kart
road 14.5 bank 1.2
land 30 0.8
hour 8

# The Marrow, deep, south of the levee; the back swamp, shallow, in the
# south-west; the breach channel cutting north through the levee.
plateau 20 20 160,300 700,300 700,420 560,400 420,396 300,398 160,404
plateau 28.7 14 210,600 460,600 470,720 210,720
plateau 21 6 356,380 394,380 394,470 356,470

